      "content": "Escrow is a neutral third party that holds funds and documents from both the buyer and seller until the home sale conditions are fully met, ensuring neither side gets their deal until both sides fulfill their obligations. If the money were simply given to the seller immediately, they could use those funds to walk away from the sale or not provide required disclosures, leaving you with no money for repairs or closing. This system protects both parties by guaranteeing that the title transfer and payment happen simultaneously and securely under the supervision of an escrow agent.",
