    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so the escrow agent is basically just a middleman to make sure everyone plays fair. how do they actually hold onto the money though? like is it just in a bank account or do they have some kind of special safe or something to keep it secure while everyone is waiting?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow agents don't use physical safes; instead, they hold the money in a specific type of bank account called an \"escrow account\" that is legally separated from their personal funds and typically segregated from the accounts of other closing agents. If an escrow agent were ever to lose or misappropriate those funds, they could be liable after paying their owed debts, which provides a layer of legal security similar to how a safety deposit box works. This banking structure ensures that the funds are maintained for a reasonable duration for all parties.",
