      "content": "Escrow agents are licensed by the state, and misusing funds can result in severe fines, criminal charges, and the loss of their license to practice. Furthermore, the strict legal terms in your purchase agreement dictate exactly when funds are withheld and when they must be released, giving you and the seller leverage to demand their return if these rules are ignored. Since escrow balances are held in a trust account, most banks even require the escrow agent to post a separate fiduciary bond to guarantee the safety of those funds.",
